# The live site's web server (deploy/laptop/README.md). Only cloudflared talks to it, on 127.0.0.1:8180;
# Cloudflare does HTTPS. Caddy serves the built frontend and passes the app's paths to the backend on 8100.
{
	admin off
	auto_https off
	persist_config off
}

http://:8180 {
	bind 127.0.0.1

	# The backend: the API, the terminal websocket, previews and VS Code (HTTP and websockets alike).
	# /metrics is left out on purpose: it is for this machine only.
	@backend path /api/* /ws/* /preview/* /ide/* /ide-fonts/*
	handle @backend {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8100 {
			# The learner's real address (Cloudflare sends it); the backend's rate limits count per address.
			header_up X-Forwarded-For {http.request.header.CF-Connecting-IP}
			header_up X-Forwarded-Proto https
			flush_interval -1
			transport http {
				read_timeout 3600s
				write_timeout 3600s
			}
		}
	}

	# The single page app: hashed assets cached for long, every other path gets index.html.
	handle {
		root * /srv/labbox/prod/current/frontend/dist
		@assets path /assets/*
		header @assets Cache-Control "public, max-age=2592000, immutable"
		@page not path /assets/*
		header @page Cache-Control "no-cache"
		try_files {path} /index.html
		encode zstd gzip
		file_server
	}

	request_body {
		max_size 10MB
	}
}
